From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcrt: Implement the _p, _s and _l printf variants and their console forms.

The printf variants that were spec stubs in msvcr80 .. msvcr120: the
stdout forms _printf_l, _printf_p, _printf_p_l, _printf_s_l, their va_list
_vprintf_* and wide _wprintf_* / _vwprintf_* forms, and the console forms
_cprintf_p, _cprintf_s (+_l), _vcprintf_p/_s (+_l) and the wide _cwprintf_*
/ _vcwprintf_*. The _p forms take positional arguments (%1$d); a format
mixing positional and plain arguments calls the invalid parameter handler
and returns -1. ucrtbase gains __conio_common_vcprintf_p/_s and
__conio_common_vcwprintf_p/_s (+_o_ forms), and msvcr120_app forwards.
msvcr110's _fprintf_s_l was a stub too.
